@page "/api-guide"
@attribute [Authorize]
<PageTitle>API &amp; webhooks · WaTenancy</PageTitle>
<div class="eyebrow">BUILD YOUR INTEGRATION</div><h1>One API. Your companies.</h1><p class="muted">Send messages from your application and consume company events through a signed webhook.</p>
<div class="guide" style="margin-top:28px"><div class="guide-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Authenticate your application</h2><p>Create an API key from your company’s API keys tab. Put it in the X-Api-Key header. The key determines the company; the caller cannot switch tenants.</p><pre>@clientExample</pre><p>Never embed API keys in public browser JavaScript. Requests are limited to 120 per minute per company. Cookies do not authenticate API routes.</p><a class="text-link" href="/openapi/v1.json" target="_blank">OpenAPI document ↗</a></section><section class="panel"><h2>Queue a message</h2><p>Each send needs a unique Idempotency-Key. Repeating the same key and payload returns the original job. Reusing it for different content returns HTTP 409.</p><pre>@sendExample</pre><p>HTTP 202 means queued. Poll GET /api/v1/jobs/{id} for status. Sent means accepted by WhatsApp; delivery and read receipts arrive later. Unknown is never automatically resent.</p></section></div>
<section class="panel"><h2>API routes</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Route</th><th>Purpose / permission</th></tr></thead><tbody>@foreach (var route in routes) { <tr><td><span class="pill">@route.Method</span></td><td><code>@route.Path</code></td><td>@route.Description</td></tr> }</tbody></table></div><p class="fine-print">List endpoints use page=1, 50 rows per page. Account control requires a key with account management permission. File uploads use the raw body with Content-Length, Content-Type and X-Filename headers. Upload file IDs can be used in a message’s fileId field.</p></section>
<div class="guide-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Configure the company webhook</h2><p>Open Webhooks in the company workspace. Save your public HTTPS URL, generate a signing secret, and enable forwarding. Click Send test event to check the complete delivery flow.</p><h3>Payload envelope</h3><pre>@payloadExample</pre><p>message.received, message.sent, message.updated and message.deleted use normalized message fields. message.receipt and chat.presence carry wacli’s original event fields. account.status reports connection changes. message.dispatch reports queued send outcomes. Voice notes and other incoming attachments include attachment metadata. Process message.media.ready to download the file from GET /api/v1/media/{id} with your company API key. message.media.failed reports exhausted download retries. Pending files return HTTP 409. WaTenancy:PublicBaseUrl sets the external origin for download URLs; otherwise resolve the relative URL against your service origin.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Verify incoming requests</h2><p>Three headers accompany each delivery:</p><ul><li><code>X-WaTenancy-Event-Id</code> — stable event ID</li><li><code>X-WaTenancy-Timestamp</code> — Unix timestamp for this attempt</li><li><code>X-WaTenancy-Signature</code> — sha256= followed by HMAC hex</li></ul><pre>@signatureExample</pre><p>Reject timestamps older than five minutes. Compare signatures in constant time. Verify the exact raw body before parsing it. Persist and deduplicate eventId before acknowledging with HTTP 2xx.</p></section></div>
<section class="panel"><h2>Delivery behavior</h2><p>Webhook events are stored before delivery. Acknowledged events show Delivered. Network errors, timeouts and non-2xx responses retry up to eight times with backoff, starting at 10 seconds and doubling. Each attempt has a 15-second HTTP timeout. Redirects are not followed. Failed deliveries can be retried manually.</p><p class="muted">Delivery is at least once and order is not guaranteed. A server restart during a request can cause a duplicate. Endpoint URL and signing secret are captured when an event is queued; rotation affects new events. A manual retry uses the current endpoint and secret. Disabling forwarding pauses queued deliveries.</p><p class="muted">Live message delivery is reconciled against the local wacli mirror every 15 seconds. Receipts and typing events are best-effort live events; WhatsApp and wacli do not provide replay guarantees for them. Pairing QR codes and session keys are never forwarded. Application history retains data for 30 days by default.</p></section></div>
@code {
    private string clientExample = "using var client = new HttpClient\n{ BaseAddress = new Uri(\"https://your-server/\") };\nclient.DefaultRequestHeaders.Add(\"X-Api-Key\", apiKey);\nvar accounts = await client.GetStringAsync(\"api/v1/accounts\");";
    private string sendExample = "POST /api/v1/messages\nX-Api-Key: wat_...\nIdempotency-Key: order-2026-1078-confirmation\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"accountId\": \"YOUR-ACCOUNT-UUID\",\n  \"recipient\": \"+27821234567\",\n  \"text\": \"Your order is confirmed.\",\n  \"fileId\": null\n}";
    private string payloadExample = "{\n  \"version\": \"1\",\n  \"eventId\": \"STABLE-EVENT-UUID\",\n  \"eventType\": \"message.received\",\n  \"occurredAt\": \"2026-10-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"tenantId\": \"COMPANY-UUID\",\n  \"accountId\": \"ACCOUNT-UUID\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"messageId\": \"WHATSAPP-ID\",\n    \"chatJid\": \"27821234567@s.whatsapp.net\",\n    \"text\": \"Hello\",\n    \"fromMe\": false\n  }\n}";
    private string signatureExample = "var bytes = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(timestamp + \".\" + rawBody);\nvar mac = HMACSHA256.HashData(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(secret), bytes);\nvar expected = \"sha256=\" + Convert.ToHexString(mac).ToLowerInvariant();";
    private (string Method, string Path, string Description)[] routes = [
        ("GET", "/api/v1/me", "Identify the authenticated company and key"), ("GET", "/api/v1/accounts", "List company WhatsApp accounts"), ("POST", "/api/v1/accounts", "Create account · manage accounts"),
        ("POST", "/api/v1/accounts/{id}/pair", "Start QR or phone pairing · manage accounts"), ("GET", "/api/v1/accounts/{id}/pairing", "Read private pairing state · manage accounts"),
        ("POST", "/api/v1/accounts/{id}/watch", "Set enabled true or false · manage accounts"), ("POST", "/api/v1/accounts/{id}/logout", "Unlink session · manage accounts"),
        ("POST", "/api/v1/messages", "Queue text or uploaded file · send"), ("GET", "/api/v1/jobs", "List outbound jobs"), ("GET", "/api/v1/jobs/{id}", "Read message status"), ("POST", "/api/v1/jobs/{id}/cancel", "Cancel a queued message · send"),
        ("GET", "/api/v1/inbox", "Read inbox and attachment metadata; optional accountId and search"), ("GET", "/api/v1/media/{id}", "Download incoming media · company key, HTTP ranges supported"), ("GET", "/api/v1/media/{id}/metadata", "Read incoming attachment status"), ("POST", "/api/v1/media/{id}/retry", "Retry a failed media download · send"), ("POST", "/api/v1/files", "Upload raw file body · send"), ("GET", "/api/v1/files/{id}", "Download uploaded attachment") ];
}

